<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Second French Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">1852 CE – 1870 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleon III's empire, which rebuilt Paris, built railways and a colonial empire, and collapsed after defeat by Prussia at Sedan in 1870.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Louis-Napoléon Bonaparte</a>, president of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-second-republic">French Second Republic</a>, seized dictatorial power in a coup in December 1851. A plebiscite approved restoring the empire, and on 2 December 1852 he became Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> III.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The early empire was authoritarian, with censorship and managed elections. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georges-eugene-haussmann">Baron Haussmann</a> rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> with boulevards and sewers, and railways, banks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> stores expanded. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, helped unify <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-savoy">Savoy</a> in 1860, but the Mexican intervention failed. From 1860 the regime liberalised, becoming a parliamentary 'Liberal Empire' under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emile-ollivier">Émile Ollivier</a> in 1870.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Provoked by Bismarck, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in July 1870. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a> was captured at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-sedan">Sedan</a> on 2 September, and two days later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-third-republic">French Third Republic</a> was proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1873.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/second-french-empire.jpg" alt="Second French Empire" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1852 CE – 1870 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Napoleon III, Empress Eugénie, Émile Ollivier</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Second Empire</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1861&amp;focus=second-french-empire" aria-label="Second French Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second French Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5175 885M5054 728L5180 883M5054 728L2321 1717"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5175 885h0M5180 883h0M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=1861&amp;focus=second-french-empire">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
